{"abstract":"Human-Robot Interaction researchers and design researchers in- creasingly recognize that they can benefit from each other’s tools, methods, and approaches. However, there are practical and episte- mological barriers to productively do so. In this demonstration we show how we, as design researchers, developed a playground for making distinctive soft robotic surfaces that can quickly be assem- bled and experienced first-hand. As such, the playground and our process serves as an exemplar of a designerly way of working with HRI.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Boer, Laurens","Bewley, Harvey"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-759394"],"event":{"acronym":"DIS","title":"ACM Conference on Designing Interactive Systems"},"filters":{"added":"2024-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Human robot interaction","Play","Prototyping","Research through Design","Social robots","Soft Robots"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a playground for soft robot design","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3656156.3665663","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-759394","identifier":[{"id":"85198901036","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-36e0b9a7-0bf1-44a3-9dc7-e5804b2d6292"],"keyword":["Human-Robot Interaction","Play","Prototyping","Research through Design","Social Robots","Soft Robots"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-9B904A1AC1170373AC0695AB3C1C74F8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/106297303/3656156.3665663.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3656156.3665663","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design, Design Research Section","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, Interaction Design Research Group","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, IxD Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Laurens","key":"boerpau","last":"Boer","locid":"25a5a0d6-404b-419c-9502-b246525617a2","name":"Boer, Laurens","orcid":"0000-0001-9723-5516","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Harvey","key":"bewleypau","last":"Bewley","locid":"5d268f64-6963-4991-9ac4-e7510c0ae705","name":"Bewley, Harvey","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"X"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Undefined"]},"sid":["itu-36e0b9a7-0bf1-44a3-9dc7-e5804b2d6292"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A Playground for Soft Robot Design","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-759394","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"This paper explores designing for mental wellbeing within the space of abortion care. We collaborated with abortion care experts, as well as design and HCI researchers, to explore different approaches to this sensitive topic. This collaboration, intertwined with our own sensitivities, and published abortion stories, informed the metaphor-driven design process detailed in this paper. Reflecting on the adoption of metaphors and their deliberate release, we propose a novel and nuanced perspective on metaphors’ role in design. The process facilitated explorations into dimensions of care, poetry, materiality, and language, resulting in the design of a care package to support self-care after abortion. By leveraging the poetic level of these metaphors, we aim to engage people's experiences through tangible and ephemeral artifacts. Finally, we discuss how this approach aided in addressing the controversial, delicate, and intimate design space of abortion while acknowledging its limitations and proposing potential future applications.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Lusi, Benedetta","Vallgårda, Anna","Bewley, Harvey","Mouritzen, Halfdan","Ludden, Geke D. S."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-789571"],"filters":{"added":"2025-02","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Netherlands"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Twente"],"keyword":["Abortion","CARE","Care Technologies","Metaphors","Research through Design"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"what we took from metaphors a case of designing for care after abortion","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3679318.3685347","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-789571","identifier":[{"id":"85206574994","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-bcb03903-b90f-4abb-a170-e7ec95bb3437"],"keyword":["Care Technologies","abortion","care","metaphors","research through design"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-3CFA40FEB0178CC775B6F85F40B25158"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3679318.3685347","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"nl","key":"university of twente","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Twente","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, IxD Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Benedetta","key":"lusipau","last":"Lusi","name":"Lusi, Benedetta","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna","key":"vallgårdapau","last":"Vallgårda","locid":"2fa5dc89-7d78-45d0-96c7-e8f39b78dd3e","name":"Vallgårda, Anna","orcid":"0000-0001-9898-8106","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Harvey","key":"bewleypau","last":"Bewley","locid":"5d268f64-6963-4991-9ac4-e7510c0ae705","name":"Bewley, Harvey","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Halfdan","key":"mouritzenpau","last":"Mouritzen","locid":"15c12622-f52e-4709-bc01-f2ff057568cf","name":"Mouritzen, Halfdan","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Geke D. S.","key":"luddenpau","last":"Ludden","name":"Ludden, Geke D. S.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"]},"sid":["itu-bcb03903-b90f-4abb-a170-e7ec95bb3437"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"What We Took From Metaphors: A Case of Designing For Care After Abortion","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-789571","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"This pictorial proposes a strategy to cultivate tensions in a design process inspired by Stengers’ notion of problematization. This strategy is a response to the issue that a current ideal is to design technology to smooth out the curves of our everyday lives rather than acknowledging our entangled relationships with all the human and non-human actors we engage with. The argument is that if we keep striving for minimal friction, we will end up estranged and discontent. The technologies will only provide a shallow technological fix that does not fit into our entangled lives. Our case is a design process to support the relationship of expecting parents. The result is a set of nine PregnancyCubes which are meant to cultivate tensions within a relationship in different ways.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Vallgårda, Anna","Wagner-Eckert, Camille","Mølhave, Caroline Bøgvad","Bewley, Harvey"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383815"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Design Tensions","Friction in Technology Design","Human Non Human Relationships","PregnancyCubes","Problematization"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"pregnancycubes a design process to cultivate tensions","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85140885795","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383815","identifier":[{"id":"85140885795","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-af205964-572b-48cd-8b5b-1ba01c105939"],"keyword":["Design Tensions","Friction in Technology Design","Human-Non-Human Relationships","PregnancyCubes","Problematization"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4FAAEA6D33AAAD33619410A9E5EDE42B"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, IxD Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna","key":"vallgårdapau","last":"Vallgårda","locid":"2fa5dc89-7d78-45d0-96c7-e8f39b78dd3e","name":"Vallgårda, Anna","orcid":"0000-0001-9898-8106","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Camille","key":"wagnereckertpau","last":"Wagner-Eckert","name":"Wagner-Eckert, Camille","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Caroline Bøgvad","key":"mølhavepau","last":"Mølhave","name":"Mølhave, Caroline Bøgvad","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Harvey","key":"bewleypau","last":"Bewley","locid":"5d268f64-6963-4991-9ac4-e7510c0ae705","name":"Bewley, Harvey","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3546155.3547284","journal":"Proceedings of NordiCHI","pages":"1","paperid":"94","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of NordiCHI"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85140885795"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-af205964-572b-48cd-8b5b-1ba01c105939"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"PregnancyCubes: A design process to cultivate tensions","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383815","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Historically, blood glucose monitoring (BGM) device design has focused on the physiological aspects of diabetes, with less consideration for the psychological aspects of relating the measurement to one's experienced symptoms. In this pictorial, we explore how the subjective experience of blood glucose monitoring can be supported. We developed the BGM diary, a training system for existing BGM devices. The BGM diary involves a practice of guessing and measuring of blood glucose, followed by an annotation of felt symptoms to facilitate learning about experiences and symptoms. We unpack how blood glucose work could involve persons with diabetes in other ways in their care program through an elaboration on the design aspects of the BGM diary and reflections with a diabetes nurse.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Boer, Laurens","Heiselberg, Kasper","Bewley, Harvey"],"cuid":["S02-082.86-029310"],"event":{"acronym":"DIS","end":"2022-06-17","place":"Virtual, Online, au","start":"2022-06-13","title":"2022 ACM Designing Interactive Systems Conference: Digital Wellbeing, DIS 2022","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Blood Glucose Monitoring","Diabetes","Self Management Technology","Subjective Experiences"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"bgm diary supporting subjective experience in blood glucose management training","src":["au","itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86846363/BGM_DIS2022_Camera_Ready_V3.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-082.86-029310","identifier":[{"id":"85133577423","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-e5a06140-1e79-4b08-b180-5f925adc4210","itu-818b9c3c-fa25-4f37-a32e-47c95e9fc110"],"keyword":["Diabetes","blood glucose monitoring","self-management technology","subjective experiences"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-41B645FCBB0725E01947A029D74B58DD"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86846363/BGM_DIS2022_Camera_Ready_V3.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, IxD Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Engineering, Department of Engineering - Socio-Technical Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Laurens","key":"boerpau","last":"Boer","locid":"25a5a0d6-404b-419c-9502-b246525617a2","name":"Boer, Laurens","orcid":"0000-0001-9723-5516","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Kasper","key":"heiselbergpau","last":"Heiselberg","locid":"80e19241-18bc-4749-a81a-5129ce88c91f","name":"Heiselberg, Kasper","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Harvey","key":"bewleypau","last":"Bewley","locid":"5d268f64-6963-4991-9ac4-e7510c0ae705","name":"Bewley, Harvey","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3532106.3533475","isbn":["9781450393591"],"pages":"1849-1862","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","series":"DIS 2022 - Proceedings of the 2022 ACM Designing Interactive Systems Conference: Digital Wellbeing","status":"p","title":"DIS '22 Companion: Designing Interactive Systems Conference"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85133577423"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-e5a06140-1e79-4b08-b180-5f925adc4210","itu-818b9c3c-fa25-4f37-a32e-47c95e9fc110"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"BGM Diary : Supporting Subjective Experience in Blood Glucose Management Training","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-082.86-029310","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Physical computing concerns the design of systems that can sense and respond to the world around them, which is why it is often used in interaction design projects in educational settings. However, students who encounter physical computing for the first time are typically not aware of the form factors and the potential for interaction of the various sensing and actuating possibilities. To complement existing touchpoints that these students have with physical computing, we present electronic smörgåsbords: boards that display collections of physical computing components that are available inhouse in an organised and interactive way to support the initiation of interaction design projects. The development of the boards allowed us to articulate four principles for their design, which are intended to inspire the development of future educational material.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Boer, Laurens","Bewley, Harvey","Cahill, Ben","Trier, Steffen Hviid"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383786"],"event":{"acronym":"TEI","title":"International Conference on Tangible, Embedded and Embodied Interactions"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Design principles","Educational tools","Electronic smörgåsbords","Interaction design","Physical computing"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"smörgåsbords for physical computing","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85746516/TEI2021_Boards_Camera_Ready2.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383786","identifier":[{"id":"85102044804","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-ada89c3c-1df8-4bd6-95a4-7a9ceedc767d"],"keyword":["Design principles","Educational tools","Electronic smörgåsbords","Interaction design","Physical computing"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B4199A54CD85746CB99EAE0C2E91A556"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85746516/TEI2021_Boards_Camera_Ready2.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, IxD Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Laurens","key":"boerpau","last":"Boer","locid":"25a5a0d6-404b-419c-9502-b246525617a2","name":"Boer, Laurens","orcid":"0000-0001-9723-5516","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Harvey","key":"bewleypau","last":"Bewley","locid":"5d268f64-6963-4991-9ac4-e7510c0ae705","name":"Bewley, Harvey","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Ben","key":"cahillpau","last":"Cahill","locid":"4b32d446-5acb-42c7-83b2-41ca287d8613","name":"Cahill, Ben","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Steffen Hviid","key":"trierpau","last":"Trier","name":"Trier, Steffen Hviid","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3430524.3446077","eisbn":["9781450382137/21/02."],"pages":"1","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"TEI '21: Fifteenth International Conference on Tangible, Embedded, and Embodied Interaction"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85102044804"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-ada89c3c-1df8-4bd6-95a4-7a9ceedc767d"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Smörgåsbords for Physical Computing","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383786","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Contemporary self-tracking devices take forms that reflect particular cultures of self-tracking that emphasize clinical perspectives and numerical precision. In this pictorial, we explore alternative forms to speculate on other possible self-tracking cultures. We present how we involved experts on the relationship between the gut and the brain to inspire a design brief for an alternative gut tracking device. This led to the design of Loupe and Lightbox, which together operate to externalize gut biota for closer examination, aesthetic appreciation, and reflection on the self. The device represents an example of self-tracking as cultivation—building a longer-term relationship with the self as something to be nurtured, tended to, and cared about.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Boer, Laurens","Bewley, Harvey","Jenkins, Tom","Homewood, Sarah","Almeida, Teresa","Vallgårda, Anna"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383724"],"event":{"acronym":"DIS","title":"ACM Conference on Designing Interactive Systems"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Gut brain axis","Gut health","Probes","Research through Design","Self Tracking Devices"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"gut tracking as cultivation","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85241372/dispx1114_boerA.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383724","identifier":[{"id":"85090499959","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-a8d3f4a1-9c48-4e63-9891-d09e6ea07413"],"keyword":["Gut-Brain Axis","Gut-Health","Probes","Research through design","Self-Tracking Devices"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E61DD573834D92716D23CBAFE85C1FE0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85241372/dispx1114_boerA.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, IxD Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Laurens","key":"boerpau","last":"Boer","locid":"25a5a0d6-404b-419c-9502-b246525617a2","name":"Boer, Laurens","orcid":"0000-0001-9723-5516","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Harvey","key":"bewleypau","last":"Bewley","locid":"5d268f64-6963-4991-9ac4-e7510c0ae705","name":"Bewley, Harvey","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tom","key":"jenkinspau","last":"Jenkins","locid":"3ad26d6b-4619-4a9f-a1b6-8424aab1dd52","name":"Jenkins, Tom","orcid":"0000-0001-6135-410X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sarah","key":"homewoodpau","last":"Homewood","name":"Homewood, Sarah","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Teresa","key":"almeidapau","last":"Almeida","name":"Almeida, Teresa","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna","key":"vallgårdapau","last":"Vallgårda","locid":"2fa5dc89-7d78-45d0-96c7-e8f39b78dd3e","name":"Vallgårda, Anna","orcid":"0000-0001-9898-8106","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3357236.3395588","pages":"561-574","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"DIS '20: Proceedings of the 2020 ACM Designing Interactive Systems Conference"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85090499959"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-a8d3f4a1-9c48-4e63-9891-d09e6ea07413"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Gut-Tracking as Cultivation","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383724","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Medical devices are moving out of the clinic and into the home. The design of these devices shapes our experience of interacting with our bodies. We attend to ovulation tracking devices that aid conception. We present Ovum; a research product that will be deployed in a long-term, qualitative study with couples trying to conceive. The contributions of this pictorial are the framing of the design space around at-home ovulation tracking devices and the presentation of our approach to this design space through working with oppositional experiential qualities by designing for fertility tracking as a shared, domestic and do-it-yourself experience.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Homewood, Sarah","Bewley, Harvey","Boer, Laurens"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382842"],"event":{"acronym":"DIS","title":"ACM Conference on Designing Interactive Systems"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Fertility Tracking","Home Medical Devices","Ovulation Monitoring","Qualitative study","User Centered Design"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"ovum designing for fertility tracking as a shared and domestic experience","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84679270/Ovum_pictorial.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-382842","identifier":[{"id":"85070585819","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-69335158-fa16-42a2-a9cc-963bd80e3b49"],"keyword":["Fertility Tracking","Home Medical Devices","Ovulation Monitoring","Qualitative Study","User-Centered Design"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-CE98EED9E4FB4C349C8B108CBAB7BAD2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url"